  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening protection in North Africa through Regional coordination and knowledge</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the capacity building support made available through past RDPP-NA Protection cycles, the IOM regional WP focuses on strengthening regional evidence and cooperation to combat trafficking inhuman beings and children on the move in North Africa. In the short term, this intervention aims to provide one up to date assessment on children on the move along Mediterranean routes, facilitate the production of tools to support cross-border protection-centred and rights-based case management for VoTs and Children on the move and create concrete coordination forum for EU, North African and key route countries&#x2019; authorities and stakeholders. In the medium term, these three effort-streams will lead to enhanced coordinated and evidence-based responses to Trafficking in Human Beings (THB) and children on the move along Mediterranean migration routes and stronger inter-governmental dialogue and exchange of practices on these topics. More specifically, a learning note on best practices in assistance and cross-border referrals of VoTs will be produced and disseminated to 200 practitioners in at least 7 countries. A training on CT data will be organized in coordination with the AU targeting 30governmental authorities from 7 countries. 1 regional meeting and 1 cross-regional coordination meeting on THB will be organized. A regional forum gathering 30 child protection and migration professionals from 6 countries will be organized to share good practices and improve dialogue on integrated child protection systems. A regional assessment of the vulnerability of children on the move in North Africa and along key corridors will be developed and a guidance for authorities on cross border case-management for children on the move produced and distributed to 150 practitioners.In the short term, this work package aims to provide one up to date assessment on children on the move alongMediterranean routes, facilitate the production of tools to support cross-border protection-centred and rightsbasedcase management for VoTs and Children on the move and create concrete coordination forum for EU,North African and key route countries&#x2019; authorities and stakeholders.In the medium term, these three effort-streams will lead to enhanced coordinated and evidence-based responsesto THB and children on the Move along Mediterranean migration routes and stronger inter- governmental dialogueand exchange of practices on these topics. This impact will be reached not only through implementation of projectactivities but also stronger synergies with other EU and EU Member States funded initiatives promoting protectionsensitive migration management in Africa implemented by IOM, and with due consideration for relevant suchinterventions led by UN agencies and EU agencies.</narrative>
  </description>
